  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY-BASED HABITAT CONSERVATION III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project ensures the sustainable management of approximately 21,000..hectares of habitat in the central highlands of Guatemala. The objectives of the..project are to: 1) restore 180 hectares of habitat via the reforestation of 200,000..native trees produced in community-managed greenhouses; 2) strengthen the..local management of 21,000 hectares of forested habitat; 3) reduce anthropogenic..pressure on habitat by (a) installing 291 fuel-efficient stoves in communities..located adjacent to the forest, and (b) reducing illegal logging in the Communal..Forest by raising awareness of the issue with a social marketing campaign and..engagement of key local stakeholders; and 4) broaden community interest and..active participation in habitat conservation.</narrative>
  </description>
